00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.300
Michael Cohen testified
in front of Congress

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.100
for over seven hours.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.653
I have some thoughts.

00:00:14.653 --> 00:00:17.070
(epic music)

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.130
Hey LegalEagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.210
Today we are covering the
testimony of Michael Cohen,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.000
President Trump's former personal lawyer

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.620
and longtime legal and extralegal fixer.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.880
Because Cohen testified for so long,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.610
I can't cover absolutely everything

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.850
that happened in the hearing.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.540
This is going to be a compilation
of the different things

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.490
that I think are particularly interesting.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.550
So I wanna point out some
of the legal principles

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.470
that I think are incredibly
important during this hearing,

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.830
but I also wanna point out
some of the rhetorical devices

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.760
that Cohen himself and Congress people

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.370
on either side of the aisle are using

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.600
to make their points and ask effective,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.890
and sometimes not effective
questions of Cohen.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.190
Now it's important to recognize

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.180
that there are several
purposes to this hearing,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.190
and it also depends on
what particular side

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.340
you're playing for.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.720
The first is to confirm or dispute

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.060
the actual testimony of Michael Cohen.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.530
So much of what he said in the hearing

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.950
was already out in the news,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.870
but there's a big difference
between speculation

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.020
about what he may testify
to and actual evidence

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.400
in the form of his testimony
on the record, under oath.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.210
The second is to get
additional information

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.110
that you had no idea existed before,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.230
the inside story that only
Michael Cohen is privy to.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.880
And so for the Democrat's perspective,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.240
I'm sure that they want
to get both evidence

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.950
of illegal conduct,

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.800
but also things that are just
embarrassing and potentially

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.880
don't necessarily rise to
the level of illegality,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.950
but are just bad for the Republicans

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.100
and the President himself.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.340
On the other hand, the
Republicans want new information

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.620
to discredit Michael Cohen
and to show the world

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.260
why no one should believe him.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.470
And the third purpose is
to get your message out,

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.670
regardless of the
testimony that Cohen gave,

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.190
you knew that a lot of the politicians

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.080
were going to grandstand,
because the world was watching

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.080
and it was a forum to
get their message out.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.760
Whether you wanted to
discredit the investigation,

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.300
or whether you wanted to bolster it.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.830
Now, as always, I want the
comments to have a vigorous

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.240
but civil discussion.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.750
Remember that Stella is
watching all of your comments,

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.530
and she wields the ban hammer of truth,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.760
so make sure all of your
comments are Stella appropriate.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.070
And smash that like button.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.980
All right, so let's dig into the testimony

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.000
of Michael Cohen in front of Congress.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.840
- Some will certainly ask
if Mr. Cohen was lying then,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.980
why should we believe him now?

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.510
- [Man] Good question.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.930
- This is a legitimate question.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.260
I had made abundantly clear to Mr. Cohen

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.793
that if he comes here today,

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:45.550
and he does not tell him the
truth, tell us the truth,

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:48.590
I will be the first one to refer

00:02:49.912 --> 00:02:52.720
those untruthful statements to DOJ.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.690
- So one of the things
that Congressman Cummings

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.710
is doing here is what
we call front-running,

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.600
which is when you know you have a bad fact

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.770
or there is bad evidence out there.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.150
The worst thing you could
possibly do is hide it

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.090
and pretend it doesn't exist.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.870
So he's getting out in
front of that bad fact

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.010
and laying the groundwork

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.430
for why we should believe Cohen now,

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.530
and trying to take the sting
out of the Republican attack.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.810
This is a classic and very
important trial tactic

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.520
that he's using here.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.380
- Mr. Trump did not directly
tell me to lie to Congress.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.423
That's not how he operates.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.080
In conversations we had
during the campaign,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.650
at the same time, I was
actively negotiating

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.760
in Russia for him.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.990
He would look me in the eye and tell me

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.820
there's no Russian business,

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.690
and then go on to lie
to the American people.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:43.640
- It's really interesting to me

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.220
that Cohen says specifically
that Trump did not

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.260
explicitly direct him to lie to Congress.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.980
You would think that if
he really was engaging

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.130
in scorched-earth tactics,

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.890
he might as well say that
Trump directed him to do it.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.290
That probably would get him a better deal

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.440
with the investigators and prosecutors,

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.260
but credibility is incredibly important.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.680
And for him to go out but not
all the way he possibly could,

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.530
that helps bolster his credibility

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.870
and helps silence critics

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.410
that he's just simply
arguing over sour grapes

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.560
about not getting a
job at the White House.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.110
- Because Mr. Trump had made clear to me

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.600
through his personal statements to me,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.000
that we both knew to be false.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.530
And through his lies to the country,

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.920
that he wanted me to lie.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.910
And he made it clear to me,

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.610
because his personal attorneys
reviewed my statement

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:37.550
before I gave it to Congress.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.220
- This is huge.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.650
I mean, this alone is quite a bombshell,

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.690
that President Trump's personal attorneys

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.080
reviewed Cohen's statement,

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.580
which is verifiably false to Congress,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.250
and is one of the reasons
that Cohen is going to jail.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.680
Number one, I would suggest
that those attorneys

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.210
lawyer up, if they haven't done so already

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.870
because it's entirely possible

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.850
that if they knew that
the changes that they made

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:03.410
to Michael Cohen's testimony were false,

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:07.430
they can be liable and
guilty of suborning perjury.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.210
And the prosecutors are able to show

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.780
that the President was aware
of and directed his attorneys

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.680
to make those changes,

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.300
that can make the President
guilty of suborning perjury.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.500
There are some pretty heavy
intent requirements there.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.210
It was recently reported
that Michael Cohen

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.800
has given Congress copies of the changes

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.490
that President Trump's
attorneys made to his statement

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:32.000
that gave rise to him pleading
guilty to lying to Congress.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.620
Those statements could
be incredibly damning.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.230
I would not expect any of those statements

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.250
to be protected by
attorney-client privilege

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.460
because I think the
joint defense agreement

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.310
has been breached.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.670
And I don't think the attorney-client

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.400
or work-product protection would apply

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.390
because of the crime-fraud exception.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.610
So if I was the President's attorney,

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.990
I would be very worried
about what those documents

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.280
show to Congress.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:56.070
- I wound up touting the Trump
narrative for over a decade.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:06:00.870
That was my job, always stay on message,

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.090
always defend.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.910
It monopolized my life.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.740
At first, I worked mostly
on Real Estate developments

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.360
and other business transactions.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.300
Shortly thereafter, Mr. Trump brought me

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.580
into his personal life
and private dealings.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.590
- A lot of people have asked me how it is

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.410
that Michael Cohen can testify
to communications he had

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:26.500
with Mr. Trump before he became President,

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.900
since Michael Cohen is an attorney

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.750
and communications with attorneys

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.390
are supposed to be protected?

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.870
Well, it's a great question,

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.470
but it's one that's very easily answered.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:37.400
Attorney-client protections only protect

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.000
communications that are made between

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.510
attorneys and their clients

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:43.720
when attorneys are acting as an attorney.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.770
If you have an attorney friend

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.680
who is working as an employee
or a business person,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.020
just because they're an attorney,

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.370
that doesn't necessarily mean

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.450
that attorney-client
privilege will attach.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.900
And Michael Cohen, for most of his career,

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.387
it appears that he was
rarely acting as an attorney

00:06:59.387 --> 00:07:03.670
and was really just acting
mostly as an extralegal thug,

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.960
and potentially as a business
person, a business associate.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.930
So all of those communications

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.050
that Mr. Cohen had with Mr. Trump,

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.600
when Mr. Cohen was not acting

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.600
in his capacity as an actual lawyer,

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.250
are not protected by
attorney-client privilege.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.060
- When he was President
of the United States,

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.080
pursuant to the coverup

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.270
which was the basis of my guilty plea

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:32.230
to reimburse me the word
used by Mr. Trump's TV lawyer

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:36.840
for the illegal hush money
I paid on his behalf.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:41.840
This $35,000 check was one
of a 11 check installments

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:45.963
that was paid throughout the
year while he was President.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:50.210
Other checks to reimburse me
for the hush money payments

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.783
were signed by Donald Trump
Jr. and Allen Weisselberg.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.560
- So this is fairly damning
evidence from Michael Cohen

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.750
that the President of the United States,

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.080
his son, Donald Trump Jr. and the CFO

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.910
of the Trump Organization all engaged

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.220
in a criminal conspiracy
to engage in election

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.580
and financial fraud by
hiding these payments

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:14.210
in order to prevent that
information from becoming public,

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:17.470
and potentially affecting
the outcome of the election.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.810
We have, of course, known about this

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.280
for quite some time now,

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.190
but Michael Cohen is going to jail

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.100
for his part in this criminal conspiracy.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.200
And it's hard to imagine
how that doesn't apply

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.370
to Donald Trump Jr., the President,

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:32.430
or Allen Weisselberg as well.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.290
Cohen states that this conspiracy existed

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.460
before the election, was
designed to affect the election,

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:41.130
and it continued into the
Presidency when Donald Trump

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:43.630
signed a personal check
while he was President.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.510
There's just no way to sugarcoat this.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.730
It's hard to see how more people
aren't going to go to jail

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.810
over this particular act, if not others,

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.630
since Michael Cohen is
already going to jail for it.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.730
- I have provided the
committee with copies of Tweets

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:01.933
that Mr. Trump posted
attacking me and my family.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:05.930
And only someone burying
his head in the sand

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.110
would not recognize
them for what they are.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:14.110
So encouragement to someone to
do harm to me and my family.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.820
- Yeah, so the Presidential Tweets

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.940
that surrounded this testimony,

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.010
including some Tweets from Congressmen

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.270
like Congressman Matt Gaetz,

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:25.760
were so borderline witness intimidation

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.010
that you have to wonder
what they were thinking

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.120
when they made those statements.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.300
Here, Cohen isn't establishing

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.530
that they constitute witness tampering,

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.760
that requires showing that the person

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:40.480
who put those statements forward intended

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.490
and had a corrupt motive

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.080
to prevent the witness from testifying.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.460
But Cohen is at least testifying

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.470
that he took those communications

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:51.140
to be a form of witness intimidation,

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.580
and was in fact intimidated by them.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.880
So, it is at least laying a groundwork

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:59.490
for further investigations
to probe what in the world

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.520
the point of those Tweets were.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.310
- How long did you work
in the White House?

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:05.850
- [Michael] I never
worked in the White House.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.350
- That's the point, isn't it, Mr. Cohen?

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.630
- No sir.
- Yes it is.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.463
- [Michael] No, it's not, sir.

00:10:09.463 --> 00:10:10.830
- You wanted to work in the White House.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:11.850
- No, sir.
- You didn't get brought

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:12.683
to the dance.

00:10:12.683 --> 00:10:13.516
- Sir--
- And now.

00:10:13.516 --> 00:10:17.910
- I was extremely proud
to be personal attorney

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:21.180
to the President of the
United States of America.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.840
I did not want to go to the White House.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.440
- So, this is a good example
of not asking questions

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.080
that you don't know the answer to.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.960
Congressman Jim Jordan here
wants to make the point

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.670
that all of this is sour grapes,

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.580
Michael Cohen wanted a
job at the White House,

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.710
he didn't get one, and
as a result he is now

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.530
turning against the President.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.460
I don't know if that's true or not,

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.880
but what I can tell you is
that he opened up the door

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.980
for Michael Cohen to opine
and give his own story

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.210
about what happened.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.430
He wanted to make a
speech, but he gave Cohen

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.100
the opportunity to directly
contradict all of the points

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.000
that he was trying to make.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.730
And on top of that,
Congressman Jordan is acting

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.030
in a fairly aggressive way,

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.450
which is a tactic that can sometimes work,

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.090
but it rarely does,
especially where the witness

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.680
is not acting hostile in any way.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.073
- How many times did
the President, Michael,

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:14.810
ask you or direct you to
try to reach settlements

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:19.340
with women in 2015 and 2016?

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:22.140
- I'm sorry ma'am, I don't
have the answer to that.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.750
I'd have to go back and try to recollect,

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.973
it's certainly the two that we know about.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:33.890
- And why do you think the
President did not provide

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.660
the accurate information in his 2017

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:41.100
financial disclosure form?

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:43.740
- So, that was a good example
of an open-end question

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.840
from Congresswoman Maloney

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.610
getting at how many mistresses Mr. Trump

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.350
had before he was elected,

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:54.780
and how many times he paid them off.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.180
She didn't get the answer
that she wanted to,

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.850
but unfortunately, she didn't
really follow up either.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.610
When a witness testifies that he or she

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.560
is not particularly sure about something,

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:05.660
you should always go back

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.830
and you should try and get the specifics.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.790
Cohen testifies that there
are at least the two.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.600
The simple follow-up question is,

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.670
are there other women
that you are aware of?

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.770
Are there other women
that he did not pay off?

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:21.290
Are there other instances that
might have led to blackmail?

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:24.260
Are there other instances
of inappropriate payments

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:29.260
to women or other people that
might have relevant testimony?

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:35.270
So often in this hearing, the
Democratic Congress people

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.840
were not listening to the
answers that Cohen was giving.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:41.360
He clearly wanted to get a story out,

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.720
whether you believe that
story is a different question.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:47.380
But he was giving them
information that they wanted,

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.670
and he probably would have given them

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.940
much, much more information
if they had just followed up.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:56.940
- You made some very demeaning
comments about the President

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.110
that Ms. Patton doesn't agree with.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:03.580
In fact, it has to do
with your claim of racism.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.220
She says that as a daughter of a man

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:09.020
born in Birmingham, Alabama,

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:13.650
that there is no way that she
would work for an individual

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.000
who was racist.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.730
How do you reconcile
the two of those, Mr.--

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.470
- As neither should I as the
son of a Holocaust survivor.

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:24.410
- There's a lot going wrong
with what Congressman Meadows

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.560
was trying to do here.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:27.810
When you have a demonstrative,

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:31.010
which effectively he was making Ms. Patton

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.870
out to be a demonstrative exhibit here,

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.470
you always have to be
worried about what people

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.510
are going to do to that.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.400
Because you're opening yourself
up to further criticism

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.160
based on the thing that
you are putting out there.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:45.900
You can't defeat an accusation of racism

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:50.190
by holding out one single black
woman who you have employed,

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:51.980
as if that defeats that accusation.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:55.510
It just simply doesn't,
it's bordering on tokenism

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.610
in and of itself.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:59.540
And number two, you don't know
how Cohen is going to react

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.010
to this particular gambit.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:02.850
This is a lawyer's worst nightmare,

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.890
Congressman Meadows really
should have thought out

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.090
the repercussions of
bringing out Ms. Patton

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.370
in this particular venue.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.570
- [Rashida] Just to make
a note, Mr. Chairman,

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.760
that just because someone
has a person of color,

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.280
a black person working for them

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:16.020
does not mean they aren't racist.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:19.460
And it is insensitive that
someone would even say racist,

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.010
say it is racism itself,

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:25.830
and to use a black woman as
a prop to prove it otherwise.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.980
And I can submit this for the record,

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.040
if a colleague is thinking
that that's what I'm saying,

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:32.847
I'm just saying that's what
I believe to have happened.

00:14:32.847 --> 00:14:34.790
And as a person of
color in this committee,

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.240
that's how I felt at that moment

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:37.820
and I wanted to express that.

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:42.180
But I am not calling the
gentleman, Mr. Meadows,

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:43.470
a racist for doing so,

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:46.460
I'm saying that in itself
it is a racist act.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.100
- Well, I hope not, Mr. Chairman,

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:49.606
'cause I need to be clear
on this particular--

00:14:49.606 --> 00:14:50.439
- [Elijah] Well, I--

00:14:50.439 --> 00:14:51.272
- Mr. Chairman.

00:14:51.272 --> 00:14:53.840
- So this is a great example
of the Streisand Effect

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:57.420
and why you don't make a
big stink about something

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.480
that you don't want to emphasize.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:02.990
Here, Congressman Meadows is
upset about the implication

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:06.730
from Congresswoman Tlaib that
he engaged in racial tokenism

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:08.410
by trotting out Lynne Patton

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:12.210
to refute the allegation
of racism by Donald Trump.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.400
Instead of letting sleeping dogs lie,

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:15.630
he makes a big deal about it,

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:17.100
which allows Congresswoman Tlaib

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.000
to read her exact same statement again

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.010
and really emphasize the point

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:25.210
that it was a stupid gambit
to make in the first place.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.950
So, if you don't want
to emphasize something,

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:29.760
don't make a huge deal about it,

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.140
that is the Streisand Effect in operation.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:37.520
- To your knowledge, did
the President or his company

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.453
ever inflate assets or revenues?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.590
- Yes.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.300
- [Lacy] And was that done

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.220
with the President's
knowledge or direction?

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.530
- Everything was done with the knowledge

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.250
and at the direction of Mr. Trump.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.450
- Now, a lot of this hearing focused on

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:57.180
asset and revenue inflation
by the Trump organization

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:00.260
for the purposes of loans
and other financial dealings.

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:01.910
When you're trying to
get a loan from the bank,

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.880
it's the bank's job to
accurately value the property

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:06.190
that's being put forth.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.930
So it's not surprising
that people try and use

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:11.010
very optimistic valuations
of their own property

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.270
in order to get a loan.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.710
However, revenue inflation is something

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:17.000
that the bank not be able to double check.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.950
The company is the one that
contains the revenue numbers.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.000
So while asset inflation
is not a good thing,

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.770
it rarely gives rise to financial fraud.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.410
Revenue inflation, on the other hand,

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:29.860
is financial fraud and could carry with it

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.860
lots of different kinds of liability.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.760
So I wish that the Congress people

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.780
had differentiated between the two,

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:38.150
because they focused
mainly on asset inflation

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.033
as opposed to revenue inflation.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:45.160
- [Virginia] So you don't
commit to changing your ways,

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:50.160
basically, because you wanna
continue to use your background

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:55.920
as a liar, a cheater, a
convicted liar, to make money.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.084
That's what you wanna do?

00:16:58.084 --> 00:17:00.784
- And that's gonna get me a
book deal and a movie deal

00:17:02.634 --> 00:17:04.410
and a spot on television?

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.940
I don't think so.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:09.130
- The Republicans focused
a lot on a potential book

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:12.780
or movie deal from Cohen,
that's an interesting tactic

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.060
for going after his bias.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.520
The more information Cohen
gives in this setting,

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:20.040
the less valuable a book or
movie deal would be later on.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.530
On the other hand, the
more famous he can become

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.100
and the more central of a player

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.210
he is in this whole scenario,

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:30.160
potentially that makes a book
or movie deal more lucrative.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.600
So, it cuts both ways,

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.270
but I'm not sure that
that means we should not

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.720
believe Cohen here.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:38.320
So I'm not sure it achieves the purpose

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.210
that they're trying to establish here.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:43.380
- The idea that a witness
would come to us who's flawed,

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:44.830
and you certainly are flawed,

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:48.400
means they can never tell the truth

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.330
and there is no validity whatsoever

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.440
to a single word they say,

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:56.800
would discredit every
single criminal trial

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.950
of organized crime in the
history of the United States.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.870
Because all of them depend
on someone who's turned.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.670
- So this hearing raises
a really interesting issue

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:06.860
that comes up in trial all the time.

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:10.260
Which is, what do you do
when you put a known liar

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.360
up on the stand?

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.530
Well, if you're the
proponent of the witness,

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.030
then you have to explain
the witness's motivation

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.510
for why they were lying before

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.020
and why they can be trusted now.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.870
And then the most
important thing you can do

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:24.320
is bolster their current
testimony with documents.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:26.900
Have independent ways of verifying

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.860
what they are testifying now is the truth.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.260
Now, if you are the other side
and you're trying to dispute

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:34.100
the evidence of someone
who has lied before,

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.800
you obviously harp on the
fact that they did in fact lie

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.400
and you should not trust them now.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.260
But you also have to establish reasons

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.720
for why they would continue
to lie at the present date.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.030
So for example, if you were dealing

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:47.890
with a confidential informant
in a criminal trial,

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.690
you'd wanna harp on the
fact that whatever carrot

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.620
the prosecution is
offering to this witness,

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:57.070
is a reason for them to
make up new information.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.810
If the confidential informant
didn't have new information

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:02.230
to give the prosecution,

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:03.850
their testimony would be worthless,

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.680
so they have an incentive
to continue to lie.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:08.970
So of course the Republicans
here are harping on the fact

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:12.950
that Cohen lied before
and cannot be trusted now.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:14.240
They have a difficult job here,

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.720
because the lies that Michael Cohen told

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.730
were for the benefit of the President,

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:21.870
especially with respect
to the length and duration

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.890
of the Trump Tower Moscow negotiations.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.030
So every time the
Republicans raise the issue

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:30.770
of Cohen's prior bad
deeds, whether it's lying

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.560
or whether it is threatening
people with lawsuits,

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.380
or whether it is illegally paying funds

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.820
to pay off porn star mistresses,

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.480
it raises the specter of who benefited

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:41.590
from all of those acts.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.680
And in almost every single instance,

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.500
the benefit of those
lies and illegal conduct

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.580
is the President of the United States.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.510
The person the Republicans
presumably want to protect.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:53.440
So I don't know if there is another theme

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:54.860
that the Republicans could have gone with

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.010
during this hearing,

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.250
but the theme that they went with,

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:01.120
which is that Michael Cohen
is a brute and a liar,

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:03.570
is true and certainly damning,

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.490
but it's also damning to the person

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.420
they're trying to protect,

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:08.740
the President in this particular case.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.950
- Is there any other
wrongdoing or illegal act

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:14.870
that you are aware of
regarding Donald Trump

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.600
that we haven't yet discussed today.

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:19.860
- Yes, and again, those are
part of the investigation

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.460
that's currently being looked at

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:23.630
by the Southern District of New York.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:27.550
- Man, so that testimony is
a bombshell in and of itself.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:31.590
Cohen has testified that he is
aware of other criminal acts

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:34.830
that surround President Trump.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.500
What I really wish the Congressman

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.060
would have done is follow up.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:42.340
He could ask, how many criminal
acts is Cohen aware of?

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.470
Whether there are other people

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.230
that had not been indicted yet,

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.050
who are responsible for
those criminal acts.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:52.510
And perhaps Cohen would
respond with the same answer

00:20:52.510 --> 00:20:54.430
that says, I can't talk about that

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:56.390
because there's an ongoing investigation

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:57.930
with the Southern District of New York.

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:00.150
But that's a good answer
for the Democrats.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.040
- And isn't it also true

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:05.620
that convicted Russian mobster Sater

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.630
even had business cards indicating

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.560
that he was a senior
advisor to Donald Trump,

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:12.510
as reported to the Washington Post?

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:13.343
- [Michael] Yes.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.480
- Did convicted Russian mobster Sater

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.200
pay rent for his office?

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.570
- [Michael] No, he did not.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.710
- So what I want point out
the Congressman is doing here

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:24.780
is he's repeating a theme.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:27.050
He's asking questions about Felix Sater,

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:30.010
and every time he says
the name Felix Sater,

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:33.960
he says convicted Russian
mobster, Felix Sater.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.520
It might sound ridiculous,

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.540
but over time it sticks in your head.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:40.190
So every time you think
of the name Felix Sater,

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.210
you're gonna think of, oh, he's
a convicted Russian mobster.

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:45.350
Of course, the person
who does that the most

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.090
is probably President Trump himself,

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.210
where he will give
nicknames to individuals

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:52.080
to engender certain ideas and emotions

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:55.640
about individuals by repeating that name

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.030
that he has created for them.

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:58.830
So that's what he's trying to do here.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.760
- [Ralph] Let me ask you this, Mr. Cohen,

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:04.760
have you legally or illegally
recorded other clients?

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:07.370
- I have recordings of people, yes.

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:08.650
- [Ralph] Legally or illegally?

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:10.750
- I believe that they're legal.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.260
- [Ralph] Did you tell him?

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:14.150
- In New York State you
don't have to do that.

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:14.983
- [Ralph] So you didn't tell him?

00:22:14.983 --> 00:22:16.460
- No, I did not.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:17.760
- These are interesting questions,

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:21.580
as a practicing lawyer
Michael Cohen recorded

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:24.210
his client's conversations with him.

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:26.700
As Cohen actually correctly points out,

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.940
New York is a one-party consent state,

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:30.910
which means the person who is recording

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:32.560
is the one that consents to the recording

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:35.340
and therefore you don't
have to notify other people.

00:22:35.340 --> 00:22:39.330
It is unusual for a lawyer
to record his clients,

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:41.830
but it may not in and
of itself be illegal.

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:43.790
If I was a client, I
certainly wouldn't want that

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:45.640
and I don't think I would an attorney

00:22:46.475 --> 00:22:48.540
who did record his clients.

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:52.210
But as an ethical violation
or as a legal matter,

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:54.350
I'm not sure that it's illegal.

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:56.870
I'd have to check, but my instinct

00:22:56.870 --> 00:23:00.100
is that in and of itself,
it's probably not illegal.

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:02.300
- [Congressman] So in
your testimony on page 13,

00:23:02.300 --> 00:23:03.277
you claim, and I quote,

00:23:03.277 --> 00:23:06.217
"Mr. Trump directed me to
use my own personal funds

00:23:06.217 --> 00:23:08.267
"from a home equity line of credit

00:23:08.267 --> 00:23:10.447
"to avoid any money
being tracked back to him

00:23:10.447 --> 00:23:12.820
"that could negatively
impact his campaign."

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:15.470
Do you have any proof of this direction?

00:23:15.470 --> 00:23:19.070
- This is always a bad
question, do you have any proof?

00:23:19.070 --> 00:23:20.970
The question assumes
that there could be one

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:22.100
single piece of evidence

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:24.410
that absolutely proves a particular point,

00:23:24.410 --> 00:23:26.280
when in reality when you're
trying to prove something

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:28.260
you use lots of tiny steps

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:30.680
to ultimately get to your end result.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:35.380
And in response to a question
of you don't have any proof,

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:37.130
the witness could just go off for days

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:39.020
about all of the different
pieces of evidence

